^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-08-24 15:08] observe — main reports 57 warnings across 381 files; one belongs to an ignored session corpus memo, leaving 56 committed-source warnings.
 >>[2026-08-24 15:12] diagnose — warnings divide into dialect false positives, sigil binding lookahead, repeated unparsed forms, three machine-frame spellings, and derived-session scope.
 >>[2026-08-24 15:15] implement — header-scoped dialect detection and colon lookahead pass 57 focused seed tests and reduce committed warnings from 56 to 53.
 >>[2026-08-24 15:17] surprise — `key: |` appears 64 times across canon; warning traces identify a missing indentation-bounded block-scalar production rather than isolated typos.
 >>[2026-08-24 15:18] taste — block scalars should become a known prose leaf with an exact indentation boundary, not a permissive rest-of-file escape hatch.
 >>[2026-08-24 15:20] verify — header-scoped dialect and sigil-binding lookahead pass 709 seed tests and TypeScript build; committed-source warnings fall from 56 to 53.
 >>[2026-08-24 15:22] implement — added a single-purpose block-scalar parser that reuses ProseChunk, deindents content, and stops before same-depth siblings or enclosing closes.
 >>[2026-08-24 15:23] verify — 712 seed tests and TypeScript build pass; recognizing the 64-use canon form reduces source warnings from 53 to 44.
 >>[2026-08-24 15:25] diagnose — final operator labels were claiming next-line identifiers as fallback modifiers, collapsing the following binding before its colon.
 >>[2026-08-24 15:26] verify — line-affine suffix parsing passes 714 seed tests and TypeScript build; source warnings fall from 44 to 33 while same-line spaced modifiers remain accepted.
 >>[2026-08-24 15:50] observe — the remaining warning corpus repeatedly confuses operational expressions, notation exhibits, and explanatory prose; common sites include bare relations, signed numbers, legacy collections, prose unions, and syntax tables.
 >>[2026-08-24 15:51] decide — quote or block-bound syntax exhibits until a first-class notation product exists; corpus frequency may propose a language feature but cannot silently grant runtime authority.
 >>[2026-08-24 15:52] verify — strict validation passes all 375 committed Spw surfaces with zero warnings after the parser repairs and convention migrations.
 >>[2026-08-24 15:54] revise — the reader note and the gap-affinity and shape-syntax plans now carry the implemented boundary rules and the open language opportunities.
 >>[2026-08-24 15:58] implement — source validation now applies the shared derived-surface contract to full paths, excluding .spw/gen products while retaining authored dotted filenames; commit review prefers the packages/spw-seed canon over the consolidated legacy tree.
 >>[2026-08-24 15:59] clarify — the earlier 375-surface strict count included ignored .spw/gen/index.spw; the source-owned corpus is 374 surfaces after the shared exclusion contract is applied.
}

